<section class="panel" aria-label="Governance and safety">
  <div class="panelInner">
    <h2 class="section-title">Governance &amp; Safety</h2>
    <p class="muted">
      Autonomy is not assumed. It's explicitly tiered — so low-risk actions can move fast, and high-stakes actions always route to humans.
    </p>

    <div class="rule"></div>

    <h3>Guardrails on AI Autonomy</h3>
    <p class="muted">
      What can safely auto-execute, what requires approval, and what must always escalate.
    </p>

    <div class="miniGrid miniGrid--4" aria-label="Autonomy tiers">
      <div class="mini">
        <b>Tier 0 — Monitor</b>
        <span>Measure, detect drift, and surface risks. No action.</span>
      </div>
      <div class="mini">
        <b>Tier 1 — Auto-execute (low risk)</b>
        <span>Reminders, routing, nudges, updates, and hygiene tasks. Logged and visible.</span>
      </div>
      <div class="mini">
        <b>Tier 2 — Recommend (approval required)</b>
        <span>Actions that affect outcomes require explicit human approval.</span>
      </div>
      <div class="mini">
        <b>Tier 3 — Escalate (high stakes)</b>
        <span>Employment-impacting decisions are never automated; governance applies.</span>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="ctaRow ctaRow--left">
      <a class="btnGhost" href="/system/core/metrics/">Read: AI-First Ops Model →</a>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="panel" aria-label="Core and change control">
  <div class="panelInner">
    <h2 class="section-title">The Core: the source of truth</h2>
    <p class="muted">
      <b>The Core prevents metric theater.</b> It's the spec layer that makes meaning stable as tools, teams, and incentives change —
      so two people don't get two answers, and "the numbers" don't shift silently.
    </p>

    <div class="miniGrid miniGrid--4" aria-label="Core scope">
      <div class="mini">
        <b>Definitions</b>
        <span>What a metric or signal means, including grain, filters, and edge cases.</span>
      </div>
      <div class="mini">
        <b>Logic</b>
        <span>Calculation + interpretation rules so two people don't reach two answers.</span>
      </div>
      <div class="mini">
        <b>Thresholds</b>
        <span>What triggers alerts, actions, escalation, or a required human review.</span>
      </div>
      <div class="mini">
        <b>Ownership</b>
        <span>Who can change what, when, and why — with simple change control.</span>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="ctaRow ctaRow--left">
      <a class="btn primary" href="/system/core/metrics/">Open the Core (spec) →</a>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
